event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dev-d002.md\", \"content\": \"This is dispatch d002.\\n\\nImplement the following in your subject repository clone (~/subject), on your own branch:\\n\\n1. Create `src/greet.py` with a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. Create `tests/test_greet.py` with unit tests covering:\\n   - A normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - The empty string (e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\")` == `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. Verify the tests pass by running, from the repo root:\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   It must exit 0. Fix anything necessary until it does.\\n\\n4. Commit both files to your own branch.\\n\\n5. Reply to this dispatch with a short summary of what you did, including the\\n   exact output/exit status of the test run.\\n\\nDo not touch any files outside src/greet.py and tests/test_greet.py unless\\nstrictly necessary to satisfy this dispatch.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

